# Source of truth for the we-are-mono/ASK commit this repo builds against.
# Single pin for kernel patches + OOT modules + userspace -- they are one
# ABI unit (cdx.ko's source consumes kernel-side FMan/DPAA headers, e.g.
# fm_ehash.h's ExternalHashTableAddKey signature, directly), so they must
# always move together, matching openwrt's `mono` branch model.
#
# History: this repo originally had the kernel side on ASK's now-deleted
# `fix/security-hardening` branch while modules/userspace were pinned to
# `mt-6.12.y` @ a211ea8 -- two different, un-cross-checked refs (see
# plans/enumerated-forging-pie.md finding #1). On 2026-09-11 both were
# bumped together to 5d96de36 (the commit then-live on we-are-mono/
# openwrt's `mono` branch). The kernel-patch side validated cleanly (Phase
# 2 of the plan above: full scratch-repo replay + real CI kernel build, 0
# failures).
#
# The OOT module side then hardware-booted with a cdx.ko that loads but
# fails its init sequence (dpa_ipsec start / scatter_gather bpool / skb_
# 2bfreed bpool init all error), so cdx_module_init() returns nonzero and
# the kernel auto-unloads it -- stripping the comcerto_fpp_send_command /
# comcerto_fpp_register_event_cb exports fci.ko needs, which then fails to
# load and crash-loops cmm. A same-day attempt to route around this by
# pinning modules/userspace back to a211ea8 while keeping the kernel on
# 5d96de36 was reverted after it failed to even COMPILE: a211ea8's cdx
# source has real ABI conflicts against 5d96de36's kernel headers
# (ExternalHashTableAddKey signature mismatch, missing struct
# ip_reassembly_info, undeclared register_dpaa_eth_bpool_replenish_hook)
# -- confirming kernel and OOT modules cannot be independently pinned at
# all. The actual fix is to debug and fix the cdx init failure at 5d96de36
# itself (compare against openwrt's working tree at the same commit),
# not to split the pin.
ASK_REPO=https://github.com/we-are-mono/ASK.git
ASK_VERSION=5d96de360d8ec7809d8b97cee0ad591e48c5e73e
